[I] Hall style stereo reverb for JACK

[T] Zita-rev1 is a reworked version of the reverb originally developed for
[T] Aeolus. Its character is more 'hall' than 'plate', and it can be used on
[T] a wide variety of instruments or voices, in stereo or Ambisonic first
[T] order B-format mode.

[U] https://kokkinizita.linuxaudio.org/linuxaudio/

[A] Kokkini Zita
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/multimedia
[F] CROSS

[L] GPL3
[V] 0.2.2

[D] 54c20515e747f6e9a58119681a8945739c855904f7eb6a058f44976e zita-rev1-0.2.2.tar.bz2 https://kokkinizita.linuxaudio.org/linuxaudio/downloads/

srcdir=*/source
var_append GCC_WRAPPER_APPEND ' ' -I$root$includedir/freetype2
var_append GCC_WRAPPER_APPEND ' ' -c?:-L$root$(pkgprefix libdir libxft)
